WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.118
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Grammar, level A one.

2
00:00:05.418 --> 00:00:08.955
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.255 --> 00:00:15.135
Unit thirty-one: Comparatives (bigger / more beautiful). Today you will compare two people or things.

4
00:00:15.435 --> 00:00:18.238
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:19.200 --> 00:00:22.479
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:23.317 --> 00:00:24.016
Bigger.

7
00:00:25.017 --> 00:00:27.167
Bigger means larger than something else.

8
00:00:27.783 --> 00:00:29.794
An elephant is bigger than a horse.

9
00:00:30.383 --> 00:00:32.664
Your turn. Say: Bigger.

10
00:00:35.500 --> 00:00:36.408
Bigger.

11
00:00:37.150 --> 00:00:37.954
Taller.

12
00:00:38.950 --> 00:00:41.182
Taller means higher than something else.

13
00:00:41.783 --> 00:00:43.133
He is taller than me.

14
00:00:43.717 --> 00:00:46.137
Your turn. Say: Taller.

15
00:00:49.000 --> 00:00:49.804
Taller.

16
00:00:50.550 --> 00:00:51.528
Faster.

17
00:00:52.517 --> 00:00:55.004
Faster means quicker than something else.

18
00:00:55.617 --> 00:00:57.512
A car is faster than a bike.

19
00:00:58.117 --> 00:01:00.885
Your turn. Say: Faster.

20
00:01:03.733 --> 00:01:04.595
Faster.

21
00:01:05.350 --> 00:01:06.514
More beautiful.

22
00:01:07.517 --> 00:01:10.608
More beautiful means nicer to look at than something else.

23
00:01:11.217 --> 00:01:13.054
This park is more beautiful.

24
00:01:13.650 --> 00:01:16.244
Your turn. Say: More beautiful.

25
00:01:19.100 --> 00:01:20.484
More beautiful.

26
00:01:21.250 --> 00:01:21.798
Than.

27
00:01:22.783 --> 00:01:25.294
Than means a word used to compare two things.

28
00:01:25.883 --> 00:01:27.140
She is older than me.

29
00:01:27.750 --> 00:01:29.868
Your turn. Say: Than.

30
00:01:32.733 --> 00:01:33.653
Than.

31
00:01:34.417 --> 00:01:35.197
Better.

32
00:01:36.183 --> 00:01:38.450
Better means more good than something else.

33
00:01:39.050 --> 00:01:40.910
Today is better than yesterday.

34
00:01:41.517 --> 00:01:44.181
Your turn. Say: Better.

35
00:01:47.033 --> 00:01:47.744
Better.

36
00:01:48.483 --> 00:01:49.426
Worse.

37
00:01:50.417 --> 00:01:52.904
Worse means more bad than something else.

38
00:01:53.517 --> 00:01:55.249
The weather is worse today.

39
00:01:55.850 --> 00:01:58.375
Your turn. Say: Worse.

40
00:02:01.233 --> 00:02:02.107
Worse.

41
00:02:02.850 --> 00:02:03.619
Compare.

42
00:02:04.617 --> 00:02:07.626
Compare means to look at how two things are alike or different.

43
00:02:08.217 --> 00:02:09.996
Compare the two pictures.

44
00:02:10.583 --> 00:02:13.561
Your turn. Say: Compare.

45
00:02:16.400 --> 00:02:17.308
Compare.

46
00:02:18.100 --> 00:02:21.739
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:22.583 --> 00:02:25.059
Visal, who is taller, you or your brother?

48
00:02:26.150 --> 00:02:35.701
My brother is taller than me. We use comparatives to compare two things. A short adjective adds -er and than: tall, taller than.

49
00:02:36.817 --> 00:02:38.538
What about longer adjectives?

50
00:02:39.650 --> 00:02:50.769
We use more before a long adjective: beautiful, more beautiful than. We do not say 'beautifuler'. Careful with the spelling: big, bigger; happy, happier.

51
00:02:51.883 --> 00:02:53.558
Are there special forms?

52
00:02:54.650 --> 00:03:04.996
Yes. Good becomes better, and bad becomes worse. They are irregular, so remember them. We never say 'more better'. Than introduces the second thing.

53
00:03:06.133 --> 00:03:07.587
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:08.450 --> 00:03:13.584
Grammar focus: Comparatives: adjective plus -er and more plus adjective plus than.

55
00:03:13.884 --> 00:03:15.013
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:15.717 --> 00:03:17.565
My brother is taller than me.

57
00:03:18.450 --> 00:03:20.949
This park is more beautiful than that park.

58
00:03:21.850 --> 00:03:23.791
Today is better than yesterday.

59
00:03:24.733 --> 00:03:32.262
Short adjectives take -er, long adjectives take more, and good and bad become better and worse. Always use than to introduce the second thing.

60
00:03:33.017 --> 00:03:36.842
Be careful! Don't say: She is more tall than me.

61
00:03:38.800 --> 00:03:41.125
Say: She is taller than me.

62
00:03:41.425 --> 00:03:43.320
Use -er with short adjectives.

63
00:03:44.133 --> 00:03:46.855
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:03:47.667 --> 00:03:48.784
Which Is Bigger?.

65
00:03:49.084 --> 00:03:51.130
An elephant is bigger than a horse.

66
00:03:52.133 --> 00:03:55.526
A car is faster than a bike, but a bike is healthier.

67
00:03:56.533 --> 00:03:59.183
Angkor Wat is more beautiful than any picture of it.

68
00:04:00.167 --> 00:04:02.329
Today the weather is better than yesterday.

69
00:04:03.333 --> 00:04:05.124
We compare two things with than.

70
00:04:06.233 --> 00:04:09.898
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:04:10.750 --> 00:04:12.784
A giraffe is blank than a dog.

72
00:04:13.084 --> 00:04:16.424
A, tall. B, taller. C, tallest.

73
00:04:19.967 --> 00:04:21.722
The answer is B: taller.

74
00:04:22.883 --> 00:04:24.662
This book is blank than that one.

75
00:04:24.962 --> 00:04:29.185
A, more interesting. B, interestinger. C, most interesting.

76
00:04:32.733 --> 00:04:35.546
The answer is A: more interesting.

77
00:04:36.683 --> 00:04:39.254
Today is blank than yesterday. (good)

78
00:04:39.554 --> 00:04:42.685
A, gooder. B, better. C, more good.

79
00:04:46.233 --> 00:04:47.943
The answer is B: better.

80
00:04:49.083 --> 00:04:50.723
Which sentence is correct?

81
00:04:51.023 --> 00:04:56.522
A, She is more tall than me.. B, She is taller than me.. C, She is taller that me..

82
00:05:00.067 --> 00:05:02.577
The answer is B: She is taller than me..

83
00:05:03.717 --> 00:05:06.784
According to the reading, what is healthier than a car?

84
00:05:07.084 --> 00:05:10.204
A, a bike. B, a horse. C, a park.

85
00:05:13.767 --> 00:05:15.418
The answer is A: a bike.

86
00:05:16.633 --> 00:05:20.133
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:05:20.983 --> 00:05:22.855
Compare two animals using 'than'.

88
00:05:31.650 --> 00:05:33.092
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:05:33.392 --> 00:05:45.860
An elephant is bigger than a dog. A cheetah is faster than a cow. A dog is friendlier than a cat in my opinion. I use -er for short adjectives and than to compare two animals.

90
00:05:46.160 --> 00:05:48.009
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:05:48.917 --> 00:05:55.621
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and comparatives: adjective plus -er and more plus adjective plus than.

92
00:05:55.921 --> 00:06:00.721
Today's value is critical thinking. Think carefully and give reasons for your opinions.

93
00:06:01.021 --> 00:06:03.731
See you in Unit thirty-two. Goodbye!

94
00:06:04.031 --> 00:06:06.823
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

